# Canary Deployment Simulator — Traffic-Ramp Policy

## Project Overview

This project implements a three-phase canary deployment policy using a pure-Python simulator.

The simulator gradually shifts traffic from the stable application version (v1) to the candidate version (v2), monitors the v2 error rate, and automatically rolls back if the error rate exceeds the configured threshold.

The objective is to reduce deployment risk by validating the candidate version before sending it all production traffic.

